<title>GERMANY: East German Oct adjusted unemployment rises.</title>
<headline>East German Oct adjusted unemployment rises.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Oct 96	 Sept 96	  Oct 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    1.097 million    1.099 million	1.034 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		1.154 million    1.143 million	1.076 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)		+11,000	+6,000) (+4,000) n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		14.7 pct     14.7 pct	 13.0 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	48,746	 48,573	   57,878</p>
<p> Vacancies		   58,551	 58,831	   58,161</p>
<p> Change in number in wrk Aug 96	 Jul 96</p>
<p>				+3,000	 +10,000 (+9,000)</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets. Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today. --Bonn newsroom, 49-228-609750</p>
</text>
